@prefix pm:      <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/ontology#> .
@prefix pmt:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/traditions/> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

#
# prima-materia — registered transmissions outside the Eurasian contact space
#
# This is the file the whole registry exists for. Every convergence the graph
# can currently state is a convergence within one connected sphere, and is
# therefore a candidate for reception rather than a finding. The witnesses
# that would change that are all here, and none of them is held.
#
# They are also the hardest to hold, and the reason is a rule of this project
# and not an accident of the material: a source must be a received work, and
# most of these transmissions were fixed in writing by someone from outside
# them. Where a corpus exists in its own language, registration names it.
# Where it does not, the entry says so, and the tradition waits for a
# decision about ethnographic first fixation that the project has not yet
# taken. Leaving them out would not have been neutrality: it would have made
# the graph report that only literate empires transmitted this knowledge.
#

# pmt:NahuaRitual has left this file: passages have been read and the
# instance now stands in traditions/nahua.ttl at pm:placesEntered, with its
# contact route corrected from absent to undecided. The correction is not a
# finding but the removal of one: the corpus was fixed a century after the
# conquest by a priest of the suppressing church, and nobody had weighed what
# that does to the transmission before the value absent was entered here.
#
# Note also that the definition this entry carried named the tonalli as a
# portion of vitality that can be lost and recovered. That is very probably
# right, and no passage for it had been read; the definition in the new file
# says only what the opened chapters say. See prima-materia#229.

pmt:MayaRitual a pm:Tradition ;
    rdfs:label "Maya ritual transmission"@en, "Maya-Ritualüberlieferung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Maya transmission of creation, of the calendar as a moving structure of obligation, and of divination by counting seeds."@en ;
    pm:principalCorpus "Popol Vuh in the Ximénez manuscript; the Books of Chilam Balam; the Dresden Codex; the Ritual of the Bacabs" ;
    pm:coverageState pm:corpusNamed ;
    pm:contactRoute pm:contactRouteAbsent .

pmt:Andean a pm:Tradition ;
    rdfs:label "Andean transmission"@en, "Andine Überlieferung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Andean transmission of huacas as animate powers, of camaquen as the vitality that animates, and of the specialists who address them."@en ;
    skos:note "The Huarochirí manuscript is Quechua prose written by Andeans at the request of an extirpator. The extirpation records are the counter-testimony, and they are in the same archive."@en ;
    pm:principalCorpus "The Huarochirí manuscript; Guaman Poma, Nueva corónica y buen gobierno; Arriaga, Extirpación de la idolatría del Perú" ;
    pm:coverageState pm:corpusNamed ;
    pm:contactRoute pm:contactRouteAbsent .

pmt:Amazonian a pm:Tradition ;
    rdfs:label "Amazonian transmission"@en, "Amazonische Überlieferung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The lowland South American transmission of songs used to direct the effect of a plant preparation, and of a body that can be exchanged for another."@en ;
    skos:note "No corpus in its own language and no writing before contact. What exists is transcribed song and ethnographic report, which this project cannot yet admit as a source. Registered so that the exclusion is visible rather than silent."@en ;
    pm:principalCorpus "No transmitted written corpus; the published icaro transcriptions and the ethnographic record stand in its place" ;
    pm:coverageState pm:corpusNamed ;
    pm:contactRoute pm:contactRouteAbsent .

# pmt:NavajoCeremonial has left this file: passages have been read and the
# instance now stands in traditions/navajo.ttl at pm:placesEntered.

# pmt:ZuniRitual has left this file: passages have been read and the
# instance now stands in traditions/zuni.ttl at pm:placesEntered.

# pmt:Midewiwin has left this file: passages have been read and the instance
# now stands in traditions/midewiwin.ttl at pm:placesEntered, with its contact
# route corrected from absent to disputed. The reason stands on the instance
# there and on the dispute node beside it.

pmt:LakotaRitual a pm:Tradition ;
    rdfs:label "Lakota ritual transmission"@en, "Lakota-Ritualüberlieferung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Lakota transmission of the seven rites, of the vision sought under fasting, and of the pipe as the instrument of address."@en ;
    skos:note "The best known account passed through two editors, and the difference between what was said and what was printed is itself documented. The tradition should enter the graph together with that dispute, not before it."@en ;
    pm:principalCorpus "Brown, The Sacred Pipe; Neihardt, Black Elk Speaks; DeMallie, The Sixth Grandfather, as the record of the mediation" ;
    pm:coverageState pm:corpusNamed ;
    pm:contactRoute pm:contactRouteAbsent .

# pmt:Ifa has left this file: passages have been read and the instance now
# stands in traditions/ifa.ttl at pm:placesEntered, with its contact route
# corrected from absent to disputed. The correction is the finding of that
# run and not a formality: one of the works read identifies the sixteen
# figures with the apparatus of geomancy, which would give the transmission a
# route to the Islamic and Mediterranean material this graph already holds.
# The reason stands on the instance there and on the dispute node beside it.

pmt:Vodun a pm:Tradition ;
    rdfs:label "Fon vodun transmission"@en, "Fon-Vodun-Überlieferung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Fon transmission of vodun as powers received into a person, with an initiation understood as a death and a return under a new name."@en ;
    pm:principalCorpus "Maupoil, La géomancie à l'ancienne Côte des Esclaves; Herskovits, Dahomey" ;
    pm:coverageState pm:corpusNamed ;
    pm:contactRoute pm:contactRouteAbsent .

pmt:KongoNkisi a pm:Tradition ;
    rdfs:label "Kongo nkisi transmission"@en, "Kongolesische Nkisi-Überlieferung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Kongo transmission of composed objects charged to act, and of the land of the dead as a place with a stated geography."@en ;
    skos:note "The Laman notebooks were written in Kikongo by Kongo authors describing their own practice, which makes them one of the few sources in this file that is not an outsider's account."@en ;
    pm:principalCorpus "The Laman notebooks in Kikongo; Laman, The Kongo" ;
    pm:coverageState pm:corpusNamed ;
    pm:contactRoute pm:contactRouteAbsent .

pmt:Bwiti a pm:Tradition ;
    rdfs:label "Bwiti"@en, "Bwiti"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Gabonese transmission of an initiation carried by a root preparation, in which the initiate is expected to meet the dead and to report the meeting."@en ;
    skos:note "The expected content of the experience is stated in advance, which makes the tradition unusually well suited to an examination of what such expectation determines."@en ;
    pm:principalCorpus "Fernandez, Bwiti: An Ethnography of the Religious Imagination in Africa" ;
    pm:coverageState pm:corpusNamed ;
    pm:contactRoute pm:contactRouteAbsent .

# pmt:AzandeOracle has left this file: passages have been read and the
# instance now stands in traditions/azande.ttl at pm:placesEntered, with its
# contact route corrected from absent to undecided. The correction removes a
# finding rather than making one: no route had been looked for. What a search
# turns up stands on both sides and is set out on the instance there. The
# control procedure this registration named is confirmed at the wording and is
# the reason the tradition was taken from the registry first; what the
# registration did not say, and what the reading added, is that the
# transmission also names eight causes to which a failure of that procedure is
# attributed, so that the condition never falls against the oracle itself. The
# count of the corroborated consultations printed in the source stands in
# examinations/azande-poison-oracle.ttl.

# pmt:Dogon has left this file: the Sirius article has been read in full and
# the instance now stands in traditions/dogon.ttl at pm:placesEntered, with its
# contact route corrected from absent to disputed. The correction is the
# finding of that run: the footnote in which the recorders themselves cite a
# French astronomical periodical of 1931 for the fifty-year period puts a route
# to the material this graph already holds at the point where the corpus was
# fixed, and the route runs through the recorders. The registration also named
# the later field re-study as part of the principal corpus, which SPEC §14
# forbids: it is a procedure with an outcome that could have gone otherwise,
# and it now stands at pm:evidenceFrom in examinations/dogon-sirius.ttl. What
# the registration called the refutation is entered as an origination and two
# protocols, not as a note. See prima-materia#250.

pmt:EthiopianOrthodoxMagic a pm:Tradition ;
    rdfs:label "Ethiopian Orthodox magical transmission"@en, "Äthiopisch-orthodoxe Zaubertradition"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Geʿez transmission of protective scrolls, of names held to bind, and of a canon that preserves works lost everywhere else."@en ;
    skos:note "African, literate, canonical, and already present in the graph at one remove: the fullest witness of the Enochic book the graph holds is the Ethiopian one."@en ;
    pm:principalCorpus "Lefāfa Ṣedeq; the asmāt scroll corpus; the Geʿez canon" ;
    pm:coverageState pm:corpusNamed ;
    pm:contactRoute pm:contactRouteDocumented .

pmt:HawaiianCosmogony a pm:Tradition ;
    rdfs:label "Hawaiian cosmogonic transmission"@en, "Hawaiische Kosmogonie"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Hawaiian transmission of a chanted genealogy of the world, recited as a continuous descent from darkness to the living."@en ;
    pm:principalCorpus "The Kumulipo in the Hawaiian text with Beckwith's edition" ;
    pm:coverageState pm:corpusNamed ;
    pm:contactRoute pm:contactRouteAbsent .

# pmt:Maori has left this file: passages have been read and the instance now
# stands in traditions/maori.ttl at pm:placesEntered, with its contact route
# corrected from absent to disputed. The reason stands on the instance there.

pmt:AustralianDreaming a pm:Tradition ;
    rdfs:label "Australian Aboriginal transmission"@en, "Australische Aboriginal-Überlieferung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Australian transmission of an ancestral order laid into country, held in song and in the routes the song follows."@en ;
    skos:note "Registered and deliberately left at corpus named. There is no corpus in the project's sense, much of the material is restricted by rules that are still enforced, and a public-domain dedication of restricted knowledge would be a taking and not an opening. The gate here protects ownership, not authority, and the project's criterion does not apply to it unchanged."@en ;
    pm:principalCorpus "No transmitted written corpus; the ethnographic record stands in its place and much of it is restricted" ;
    pm:coverageState pm:corpusNamed ;
    pm:contactRoute pm:contactRouteAbsent .

pmt:SiberianShamanism a pm:Tradition ;
    rdfs:label "Siberian shamanic transmission"@en, "Sibirische Schamanenüberlieferung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Tungus and Sakha transmission of an office entered through an illness that resolves only on acceptance, with a costume, a drum and a stated itinerary."@en ;
    skos:note "The region the word shaman was taken from. The graph uses the category and holds no witness from its source."@en ;
    pm:principalCorpus "Shirokogoroff, Psychomental Complex of the Tungus; the published Olonkho epics; Anisimov's field records" ;
    pm:coverageState pm:corpusNamed ;
    pm:contactRoute pm:contactRouteUndecided .

# pmt:InuitAngakkuq has left this file: passages have been read and the
# instance now stands in traditions/inuit-angakkuq.ttl at pm:placesEntered,
# with its contact route corrected from absent to disputed. The reason stands
# on the instance there. The account of qaumaneq that this registration named
# lies beyond the portion of the volume the run could reach and is not yet in
# the graph; see prima-materia#99.

pmt:SamiNoaidi a pm:Tradition ;
    rdfs:label "Sámi noaidi transmission"@en, "Samische Noaidi-Überlieferung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Sámi transmission of the drum as an instrument of divination and of a journey undertaken while the body lies still."@en ;
    skos:note "Recorded almost entirely by missionaries engaged in suppressing it, which makes every passage a hostile witness and the hostility itself a datum."@en ;
    pm:principalCorpus "Leem, Beskrivelse over Finmarkens Lapper; the eighteenth-century missionary manuscripts of Skanke and Randulf" ;
    pm:coverageState pm:corpusNamed ;
    pm:contactRoute pm:contactRouteUndecided .
